# Deployment & Maintenance Rules

## Environment Management

### Environment Configuration
- **Environment Variables**: Use .env files for environment-specific configuration
- **Environment Separation**: Maintain separate configurations for development, staging, and production
- **Secret Management**: Store sensitive data in environment variables, never in code
- **Configuration Validation**: Validate environment configuration on application startup

### Build Process
- **Build Scripts**: Maintain clean, reproducible build processes
- **Build Optimization**: Optimize builds for production (minification, compression)
- **Asset Pipeline**: Use consistent asset processing and optimization
- **Build Verification**: Verify builds work correctly before deployment

### Version Control
- **Meaningful Commits**: Use descriptive commit messages following conventional commits
- **Branch Strategy**: Use consistent branch naming and management strategies
- **History Management**: Maintain clean git history with logical commit grouping
- **Tag Management**: Use semantic versioning and proper release tagging

## Deployment Standards

### Deployment Process
- **Automated Deployment**: Use automated deployment pipelines where possible
- **Rollback Strategy**: Maintain ability to quickly rollback deployments
- **Health Checks**: Implement health checks to verify successful deployments
- **Deployment Monitoring**: Monitor deployments for issues and performance

### Production Readiness
- **Performance Optimization**: Ensure production builds are optimized for performance
- **Security Hardening**: Apply security best practices for production environments
- **Error Handling**: Implement comprehensive error handling for production
- **Monitoring Setup**: Set up monitoring and alerting for production systems

### Backup Strategy
- **Regular Backups**: Maintain regular backups of critical data and configurations
- **Backup Verification**: Regularly verify backup integrity and restore capabilities
- **Disaster Recovery**: Maintain disaster recovery procedures and documentation
- **Data Retention**: Implement appropriate data retention policies

## Monitoring & Maintenance

### Performance Monitoring
- **Core Web Vitals**: Monitor Core Web Vitals and performance metrics
- **Real User Monitoring**: Track actual user experience and performance
- **Resource Monitoring**: Monitor server resources and application performance
- **Alerting**: Set up alerts for performance degradation and issues

### Error Tracking
- **Error Logging**: Implement comprehensive error logging and tracking
- **Error Analysis**: Regularly analyze error patterns and trends
- **User Feedback**: Collect and analyze user feedback on issues
- **Issue Resolution**: Maintain processes for quick issue resolution

### Maintenance Procedures
- **Regular Updates**: Keep dependencies and libraries updated
- **Security Patches**: Apply security patches promptly
- **Performance Optimization**: Continuously optimize based on monitoring data
- **Documentation Updates**: Keep documentation current with system changes

## Code Quality for Deployment

### Pre-Deployment Checks
- **Code Review**: Ensure all code changes are reviewed before deployment
- **Testing**: Run comprehensive tests before deployment
- **Security Scan**: Perform security scans on code and dependencies
- **Performance Testing**: Test performance impact of changes

### Post-Deployment Verification
- **Functionality Testing**: Verify all functionality works correctly after deployment
- **Performance Monitoring**: Monitor performance after deployment
- **Error Monitoring**: Watch for new errors or issues after deployment
- **User Feedback**: Monitor user feedback after deployment

### Rollback Procedures
- **Quick Rollback**: Maintain ability to quickly rollback problematic deployments
- **Data Integrity**: Ensure rollbacks don't cause data loss or corruption
- **Communication**: Communicate rollbacks to stakeholders
- **Post-Rollback Analysis**: Analyze issues that led to rollback

## Security & Compliance

### Security Standards
- **Access Control**: Implement proper access controls and authentication
- **Data Protection**: Ensure sensitive data is properly protected
- **Audit Logging**: Maintain audit logs for security and compliance
- **Vulnerability Management**: Regularly scan for and address vulnerabilities

### Compliance Requirements
- **Regulatory Compliance**: Ensure compliance with relevant regulations
- **Data Privacy**: Implement appropriate data privacy controls
- **Documentation**: Maintain compliance documentation and procedures
- **Regular Audits**: Conduct regular compliance audits and reviews

## Documentation & Knowledge Management

### Deployment Documentation
- **Deployment Procedures**: Document deployment procedures and checklists
- **Configuration Management**: Document configuration management procedures
- **Troubleshooting Guides**: Maintain troubleshooting guides for common issues
- **Runbooks**: Create runbooks for operational procedures

### Knowledge Transfer
- **Team Training**: Provide training on deployment and maintenance procedures
- **Documentation Updates**: Keep documentation current with system changes
- **Best Practices**: Share best practices and lessons learned
- **Continuous Learning**: Encourage continuous learning and improvement

### Change Management
- **Change Documentation**: Document all changes and their impact
- **Change Communication**: Communicate changes to stakeholders
- **Change Testing**: Test changes thoroughly before implementation
- **Change Review**: Review changes for potential issues and improvements
